<script data-rh="true" id="seo-schema-0" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"What Are Your Streams Actually Worth in 2026? The Complete Breakdown","description":"Compare per-stream rates for Spotify, Apple Music, Tidal, YouTube Music, Amazon Music, Deezer & SoundCloud in 2026. Learn what your catalog is really worth beyond streaming.","url":"https://spacemusic.io/guides/what-are-your-streams-worth-2026/","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"SPACE","url":"https://spacemusic.io"}}</script>
<script data-rh="true" id="seo-schema-1" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Spotify pay per stream in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Spotify pays between $0.003 and $0.005 per stream in 2026. The exact rate depends on the listener's country, whether they use the free or premium tier, and total platform-wide streaming volume that month. At the midpoint of $0.004 per stream, you'd need 250,000 streams to earn $1,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a music stream worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A single music stream is worth between $0.002 (SoundCloud/YouTube) and $0.013 (Tidal) depending on the platform. However, the true value of your streams lies in what they say about your catalog's worth as an asset. Predictable, recurring streaming revenue can be valued at 4-10x annual earnings, meaning a catalog earning $5,000/year could have a lump-sum value of $20,000–$50,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do artists get paid per 1,000 streams?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Per 1,000 streams: Spotify pays $3–$5, Apple Music pays $7–$10, Amazon Music pays $4–$8, Tidal pays $8–$13, YouTube Music pays $2–$5, Deezer pays $4–$7, and SoundCloud pays $2–$4. These are gross platform rates before your distributor takes their cut (typically 10-20%)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Apple Music pay per stream compared to Spotify?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Apple Music pays roughly 2x more per stream than Spotify — $0.007–$0.01 vs $0.003–$0.005. The difference is because Apple Music has no free tier; every listener pays for a subscription. However, Spotify's much larger user base (626M vs 98M) means most artists earn more total revenue from Spotify despite the lower per-stream rate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my streaming royalties?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Music catalog sales — where you sell some or all of your streaming royalty rights for a lump-sum payment — are increasingly common for independent artists. Buyers like SPACE acquire catalogs at multiples of annual streaming revenue (typically 4-10x for independent artists). You can sell your entire catalog, specific albums, or even partial rights while retaining some ownership."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is my music catalog worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your catalog's value is typically calculated as a multiple of your trailing 12-month net streaming revenue. For independent ambient, lo-fi, and mood music catalogs, multiples range from 4x (declining revenue) to 10x (growing revenue with diverse platform distribution). A catalog earning $6,000/year is typically worth $24,000–$60,000 as a lump-sum sale. Use SPACE's free calculator for a personalized estimate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which streaming platform pays artists the most?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Tidal pays the most per stream at $0.008–$0.013, followed by Apple Music at $0.007–$0.01. However, 'most' depends on whether you're measuring per-stream rate or total revenue. Spotify pays the least per stream but generates the most total revenue for most artists due to its massive user base. The optimal strategy is diversified distribution across all platforms."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do ambient and lo-fi artists earn less per minute from streaming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Streaming platforms count a stream after 30 seconds of listening and pay the same amount regardless of track length. A 2-minute pop track and a 10-minute ambient piece earn identical per-stream payouts, meaning ambient artists earn roughly 80% less per minute of content consumed. This structural disadvantage is one reason ambient catalog sales — which value total revenue rather than per-stream economics — can be more financially advantageous for ambient creators."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between pro-rata and user-centric streaming payments?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pro-rata (used by Spotify, Apple Music, Amazon) pools all subscription revenue and divides it by total platform streams. Your share depends on your proportion of total streams. User-centric (used by Tidal, SoundCloud) distributes each subscriber's fee only to the artists they listened to. User-centric models benefit niche artists with dedicated fans, while pro-rata favors mainstream artists with massive stream counts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I increase my streaming revenue as an independent artist?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Three strategies: (1) Diversify across platforms — don't rely solely on Spotify. Apple Music pays 2x more per stream, and Amazon's Alexa drives ambient streams. (2) Optimize for playlists — submit to editorial playlists, create your own, and engage with curators. (3) Consider catalog monetization — rather than waiting years for streams to accumulate, a catalog sale can unlock the full value of your music immediately at 4-10x annual revenue."}}]}</script>
<script data-rh="true" id="seo-schema-2" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://spacemusic.io/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Guides","item":"https://spacemusic.io/guides/what-are-your-streams-worth-2026/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"What Are Your Streams Actually Worth in 2026? The Complete Breakdown","item":"https://spacemusic.io/guides/what-are-your-streams-worth-2026/"}]}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/journey-cta-632796e93c26.css"></head>

